# This branch is source only: .tex for Y1S2, .md for Y1S1, and nothing else.
# Everything the build produces lives on the gh-pages branch, and every binary
# lives either there or in Google Drive. The rules below keep it that way — a
# blanket `git add -A` must not be able to sweep generated output back in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated --
# The built site. One page per topic, plus the hubs and the shared shell.
*.html
*.css
*.woff2
assets/

# Web copies of the figures, emitted beside each chapter by the pipeline.
media/

# Portable Markdown written from the Y1S2 .tex. Generated, and nothing links
# it, so it is not published in either place.
y1s2/**/chapters*/*.md

# Intermediate .tex emitted by the figure pre-renderers; publish.ps1 deletes and
# regenerates it on every run, so a committed copy would only ever be stale.
*.gen.tex

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ figures --
# Y1S1's figures live at chapters/images/ as .webp and ARE published: that path
# is correct both for pandoc (relative to its working directory) and for
# GitHub's viewer (relative to the .md), so the notes render wherever they are
# read. Encoded losslessly from the PNGs at roughly a quarter the size.
#
# What is excluded is the raster originals, wherever they sit — the Y1S1 PNGs
# these .webp were made from, and the Y1S2 figures that only pdflatex consumes.
# Note this cannot be written as `images/`: that would match chapters/images/
# too, since a bare directory pattern matches at every level.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# Pre-rendered bytefield/TikZ figures. Y1S2 only, and consumed by the .gen.tex
# the pre-renderers emit, so they are build intermediates rather than source.
*.svg

# Disables Jekyll on GitHub Pages. It belongs beside the HTML, on gh-pages.
.nojekyll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- artefacts --
# Compiled PDFs live in Google Drive — large binaries, regenerated on every
# LaTeX build, so committing them would grow history without bound.
*.pdf

# LaTeX build by-products.
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# Stray output directory from a LaTeX invocation where %OUTDIR% went unexpanded.
%OUTDIR%/

# Python bytecode from the pipeline's renderers.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- machinery --
# The shared LaTeX -> HTML/Markdown build. Kept locally: this repo publishes the
# notes, not the tooling that renders them.
web-pipeline/

# AI-assistant authoring notes. Scaffolding rather than notes.
CLAUDE.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/

# Build configuration for the web pipeline: per-course branding/navigation
# (course.yml), the topic manifest (site.psd1), and the hub metadata (hub.yml).
# Inputs to web-pipeline/, which is itself ignored.
course.yml
site.psd1
hub.yml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- drafts --
# Work in progress, not ready to publish. y2s1 has no hub.yml, so publish-hub.ps1
# cannot build a semester page for it and it does not appear on the root chooser.
# Remove the line when the semester is ready to go live.
y2s1/
system-design/

# ---------------------------------------------------------- OS / editor noise --
image.png
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
